A||N||4||polomeno||quick head gasket question !||||1||
Z||000000||polomeno||04-03-2001||01:43 PM||||hey guys i went to order the parts i need to do a head gasket job.. the guy at parts place at dealership said i can use 85 head bolts for a 84 engine? 4 banger.. also he asked if i wanted a "cross flow' head gasket ?? what exactly should i ask for , for my 84 sport coupe ?<P>thanks<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000001||polomeno||04-03-2001||03:01 PM||||anyone??||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||04-03-2001||04:50 PM||||AFAIK, all 4 cyl Fiero heads are crossflow (intake on one side, exhaust on the other). Don't know why he would have asked you that.<BR>Not sure about the bolts. Can't think of any reason that they shouldn't work. Seems like replacement of 84 headbolts might have even been a recall item. Check link for Ogre's Cave at the bottom of the page. He's got tons of useful info.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-03-2001||08:03 PM||||Don't reuse any of the old bolts. They are known to be weak. The exhaust side bolts were part of the recall but at this point you need to replace the whole set.<P>The original 84 bolts are no longer available. The new bolts are "torque to yield." You turn them to X foot pounds then Y degrees. You need a torque wrench and an angle gauge. Tourque them as directed using the 85/86 tables.(Warning: the torque isn't the same for every bolt. read the torque table & bolt map carefully.)<P>The new TTY bolts stretch as they are tightened. They can only be used once.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||polomeno||04-03-2001||08:17 PM||||Thanks guys! that's what i needed to know  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
